    "summary": "Model regenerated successfully and passed L1/L2/L3 checks.\n\nRoot cause of the L2-1 failure: the accepted decision support.3.dofs had longitudinal = \"spring\" for abutment 3, but abutment 3 carries PTFE sliding laminated elastomeric bearings (bearing:3 sliding=true, support.3.Kh already accepted as 0). Per MR-03 a sliding bearing must have longitudinal free (Kh=0). The instance was correct; the decision was wrong. Re-proposed support.3.dofs = {vertical: spring, longitudinal: free, rotation: free} (evidence MR-03, dec:support.3.bearing, inst:bearing:3), then regenerate_model succeeded.\n\nModel summary: 3-span continuous spine-beam (2D) unit, 20+25+20 m, four C50 precast small-box girders (A=1.0605 m², I=0.2517 m⁴ each; girder.A=4.242, girder.I=1.007, Ec=34500 MPa, γ=26 kN/m³, self-weight only). Rigid/spring supports: abutments 0 and 3 and pier 2 with PTFE sliding bearings (longitudinal free) and pier 1 with plain elastomeric fixed bearings (longitudinal spring, Kh=26250 kN/m); all vertical springs (Kv≈1.133e7 kN/m per line), rotation free. Highway Class I, three lanes, carriageway 11.5 m, impact factor μ=0.288 (from f1=5.573 Hz).\n\nKey results: first three vertical frequencies 5.573 / 8.426 / 10.186 Hz; self-weight reactions ≈ 820 / 2764 / 2764 / 820 kN; self-weight midspan moments ≈ 2690 / 2968 / 2690 kNm and support moments ≈ -5649 kNm; governing live-load positive moment 5341 kNm (span 2) and negative moment -3864 kNm (over pier 1)."
